# Opus's D1, folded into FABLE-SONNET-NODE-ROOT-20260923-121: a typed-
# formal path root must read the ARGUMENT's value, not the unit's static
# declaration child for the formal's type. Before the fix, get(a) read
# the Model declaration site (value 1) instead of a's own value (5).
# Spelled exactly as fable required -- `return: x\value` -- exercising
# fix (b) in the same ticket: a field path is an ordinary expression
# value, not gated on the statement head being a declared own field
# (l2_emit_body's value-position join-path dispatch used to refuse this
# shape unconditionally with "a field path value needs a declared
# destination", for ANY root, reproduced with a plain own-field root too
# -- a different gap than D1, now fixed here per fable's instruction).
Model:
    size_t: value 1U
end: Model

fn: get (Model: x) size_t
    return: x\value

Model: a
a\value: 5U
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: get(a); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
